{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "F12bRecurrenceViaAMakearrayRegion",
    "description": "REPRO, EXPECTED TO FAIL. F12's second spelling: the recurrence written as a `makearray` whose FIRST region is the base case and whose second region reads the array being assembled one position back. The same recurrence F12 asks for -- s[1] = 1, s[k] = 2*s[k-1], answer [1, 2, 4, 8] -- so the four spellings are directly comparable.\n\nThis is not the same node as F12's `aggregate`, and it is the spelling an author reaches for next, because `makearray`'s regions are explicitly ordered and its overlap rule is `later entries overwrite earlier ones` (esm-spec \u00a74.3.2) -- which reads like a licence to define position k from position k-1. It is not one: the region ORDER governs which write wins, not the order in which cells are evaluated, and the assembled array is still one value computed from its operands.\n\nIt validates, and then fails exactly as F12's aggregate does:\n\n    assertion evaluation failed: array state 's' has no cells in var_map\n\nRecorded separately because a reader who has only seen F12 cannot tell whether the limitation is in `aggregate` or in self-reference itself. It is the latter: BOTH array-producing nodes refuse it, and for the same reason.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "finding",
      "expected-to-fail",
      "makearray",
      "recurrence"
    ]
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "step_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 4
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "F12bRecurrenceViaAMakearrayRegion": {
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-12
      },
      "variables": {
        "s": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "step_rows"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 at the first step, twice the previous value at every later one."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "s",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "makearray",
            "args": [],
            "regions": [
              [
                [
                  1,
                  1
                ]
              ],
              [
                [
                  2,
                  4
                ]
              ]
            ],
            "values": [
              1.0,
              {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "args": [],
                "output_idx": [
                  "k"
                ],
                "ranges": {
                  "k": [
                    2,
                    4
                  ]
                },
                "expr": {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "s",
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "k",
                            1
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    2.0
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "a_recurrence_in_a_makearray_region_evaluates",
          "description": "INTENDED behaviour: [1, 2, 4, 8].",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "s",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "step_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "s",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 2.0,
              "coords": {
                "step_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "s",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 8.0,
              "coords": {
                "step_rows": 4
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
